---
layout: layouts/base.njk
wrap: report-wrap
schemas:
  - published-report
pagination:
  data: published.entries
  size: 1
  alias: entry
permalink: "{{ entry.url }}"
---
{%- import "partials/report-macros.njk" as R -%}
{%- from "partials/bot-mark.njk" import botMark -%}
{%- from "partials/country-flag.njk" import countryFlag -%}
{%- set s = p.strip -%}
{%- set cc = p.claimCard -%}
<article class="report-doc">

<div class="rd-tags">
  <span class="badge {{ report.verdict | verdictClass }}">{{ report.verdict | verdictLabel }}</span>
  {%- if report.clusterName %}<a class="tile" href="{{ ('/registry/cluster/' + (report.clusterName | slugify) + '/') | loc(lang) | url }}">{{ report.clusterName }}</a>{% endif %}
  {%- if report.splice %}<a class="tile" href="{{ ('/registry/splice/' + (report.splice | slugify) + '/') | loc(lang) | url }}">Splice {{ report.splice }}</a>{% endif %}
</div>

{# ============================================================ hero card #}
<div class="hero-card">
  <div class="hero-l">
    <div class="klass"><span class="kdot"></span>{{ splice.klass }}</div>
    <h1 class="claimq">{{ cc.falseClaim | defangCopy | safe if cc.falseClaim else report.label }}</h1>
    <div class="finding">
      <span class="badge b-f">{{ report.verdict | verdictLabel }}</span>
      <p><b>{{ finding.lead | defangCopy | safe }}</b>{% if finding.rest %} {{ finding.rest | defangCopy | safe }}{% endif %}</p>
    </div>
    {%- if truth.text %}
    <div class="truth">
      <div class="lbl">What actually happened</div>
      <p>{{ truth.text | defangCopy | safe }}</p>
      {%- if truth.src %}<div class="src">{{ truth.src | defangCopy | safe }}</div>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- set reportUrl = site.url + page.url %}
    <div class="tools">
      <details class="toolpop">
        <summary>Share</summary>
        <div class="pop">
          <div class="popurl">{{ reportUrl }}</div>
          <a href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text={{ (finding.lead or report.label) | urlencode }}&url={{ reportUrl | urlencode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Share on X</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url={{ reportUrl | urlencode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Share on LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="mailto:?subject={{ ('Citere claim report — ' + report.claimKey) | urlencode }}&body={{ reportUrl | urlencode }}">Email a link</a>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="toolpop">
        <summary>Export</summary>
        <div class="pop">
          <a href="{{ ('/registry/' + report.slug + '.json') | url }}" download>JSON — full report</a>
          <a href="{{ ('/registry/' + report.slug + '.csv') | url }}" download>CSV — per-bot cells</a>
        </div>
      </details>
      {%- if "countermeasures" not in hidden %}<a href="#countermeasures">Countermeasures ↓</a>{% endif %}
      <a href="#card">Claim card ↓</a>
      <span class="ref">Claim {{ report.claimKey }}{% if p.meta.trackedSince %} · tracked since <time datetime="{{ p.meta.trackedSince }}">{{ p.meta.trackedSince | displayDate }}</time>{% endif %}{% if p.euvs %} · {% if p.euvs.url %}documented by <a href="{{ p.euvs.url }}" rel="nofollow">EUvsDisinfo</a>{% else %}documented by EUvsDisinfo{% endif %}{% endif %}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-r">
    <h2>Which chatbots repeat it</h2>
    <p class="ssub">Share of answers stating the fake as fact{% if p.meta.countries | length %} · {{ p.meta.countries | length }} {{ "country" if p.meta.countries | length == 1 else "countries" }}{% endif %}{% if personaCount %} · {{ personaCount }} question types{% endif %}</p>
    {%- if not heroBots | length %}<div class="rd-empty">No judged answers yet.</div>
    {%- else %}
      {%- for b in heroBots %}
      <div class="brow">
        <div class="bname">{{ botMark(logos, b.slug, "sm") }}<span>{{ b.label }}</span></div>
        <div class="btrack"><div class="bfill" style="width:{{ b.fillPct | round(1) }}%"></div><div class="bsrc" style="width:{{ b.srcPct | round(1) }}%"></div></div>
        <div class="bval"><b>{{ b.pct }}%</b><span>{{ b.repeats }} of {{ b.answers }}{% if b.criticalCited %} · {{ b.criticalCited }} sourced{% endif %}</span></div>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
      <div class="legend"><span><i style="background:#a4adba"></i>Repeated the fake</span><span><i style="background:var(--false)"></i>…and cited a listed source</span></div>
      {%- if heroInsight %}<div class="insight"><b>{{ heroInsight.count }}</b>{{ heroInsight.rest }}</div>{% endif %}
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</div>

{# ============================================================ six-tile KPIs #}
<div class="kpis">
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ s.botsTested }}</b><span>chatbots tested</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ s.answers }}</b><span>answers · {{ s.countries }} {{ "country" if s.countries == 1 else "countries" }}</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b class="{{ 'bad' if s.repeatedFake }}">{{ s.repeatedFake }}</b><span>repeated the fake</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b class="{{ 'bad' if s.critical }}">{{ s.critical }}</b><span>critical: repeated + cited a listed source</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ s.sourcesIdentified }}</b><span><a href="#sources">disinformation sources identified</a></span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b class="{{ 'mute' if not countermeasuresTaken }}">{{ countermeasuresTaken }}</b><span><a href="#countermeasures">countermeasures taken</a></span></div>
</div>

{# ============================================================ summary / response #}
{%- if ("summary" not in hidden) and (analyst.summary or analyst.response) %}
<section class="summary-sec">
  <div class="summary">
    {%- if analyst.summary %}
    <div class="pnl"><div class="lbl">Summary</div>{{ analyst.summary | md | defangCopy | safe }}</div>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if analyst.response %}
    <div class="pnl"><div class="lbl">Our response</div>{{ analyst.response | md | defangCopy | safe }}</div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# ============================================================ sticky section nav #}
<nav class="secnav" aria-label="Report sections">
  {%- if "why" not in hidden %}<a href="#why">Why this is false</a>{% endif %}
  {%- if "bots" not in hidden %}<a href="#bots">What the chatbots did</a>{% endif %}
  {%- if "evidence" not in hidden %}<a href="#evidence">Evidence</a>{% endif %}
  {%- if "sources" not in hidden %}<a href="#sources">Sources</a>{% endif %}
  {%- if "countermeasures" not in hidden %}<a href="#countermeasures">Countermeasures</a>{% endif %}
  {%- if "card" not in hidden %}<a href="#card">Claim card</a>{% endif %}
  {%- if ("appendix" not in hidden) and (p.resultsByBot.cells | length or p.axb.validTotal or p.live or p.trend) %}<a href="#appendix">Data appendix</a>{% endif %}
  {%- if "limitations" not in hidden %}<a href="#limitations">Limitations</a>{% endif %}
  {%- if "method" not in hidden %}<a href="#method">Method</a>{% endif %}
</nav>

{# ============================================================ why this is false #}
{%- if "why" not in hidden %}
<section id="why" class="flat">
  <h2>Why this is false</h2>
  <div class="grain">
    <div class="ic">✓</div>
    <div>
      <div class="lbl">Grain of truth</div>
      {%- if whyFalseText.realEvent %}<p>{{ whyFalseText.realEvent | defangCopy | safe }}</p>{% else %}<p class="rd-dim">Grain of truth not filled on the claim card.</p>{% endif %}
      {%- if p.whyFalse.grainFacts | length %}
      <ul class="grainlist">{% for g in p.whyFalse.grainFacts %}<li>{{ g.fact | defangCopy | safe }}{% if g.source %} — {{ R.sourceRef(g.source) }}{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if p.whyFalse.debunkArgument | length %}
  <div class="debunk">
    <div class="hd f">The fake says</div><div class="hd t">What is true</div><div class="hd">Evidence</div>
    {%- for d in p.whyFalse.debunkArgument %}
    <div class="cell f">{{ d.assertion | defangCopy | safe }}</div><div class="cell">{{ d.refutation | defangCopy | safe }}</div><div class="cell e">{{ R.sourceRef(d.source) }}</div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  {%- else %}<div class="rd-empty">No debunk argument yet — add fake-says / what-is-true rows on the claim card.</div>{% endif %}

  {%- if splice.letter or whyFalseText.whyItWorks or chainNodes | length %}
  <div class="howbuilt">
    <div class="pnl">
      <h3>How the lie is built</h3>
      {%- if splice.letter %}<div class="splice"><span class="sl">Type {{ splice.letter }}</span><b>{{ splice.phrase }}</b></div><p class="sdef">{{ splice.def }}</p>{% endif %}
      {%- if whyFalseText.whyItWorks %}<p><b>On this claim:</b> {{ whyFalseText.whyItWorks | defangCopy | safe }}</p>{% else %}<p class="rd-dim">Add the removed element on the claim card to explain how this specific lie is built.</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="pnl">
      <h3>How it moved</h3>
      <p class="ssub">From publisher to chatbot</p>
      {%- if chainNodes | length %}
      <div class="flow">{% for n in chainNodes %}<div class="fs {{ 'src' if not n.last }}"><div class="card"><div class="d">{{ n.date }}</div><div class="ttl">{{ n.node | defang if n.isDomain else n.node }}</div>{% if n.injection %}<p class="rd-crit">injection line</p>{% endif %}</div></div>{% endfor %}</div>
      {%- else %}<div class="rd-empty">No distribution chain recorded — add surface objects on the claim card.</div>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# ============================================================ what the chatbots did #}
{%- if "bots" not in hidden %}
<section id="bots" class="flat">
  <h2>What the chatbots did with it</h2>
  <p class="intro">We asked {{ s.botsTested }} chatbots about this claim{% if p.meta.countries | length %} in {{ p.meta.countries | length }} {{ "country" if p.meta.countries | length == 1 else "countries" }}{% endif %}, phrasing the question four ways: as someone who knows nothing, as someone following the news, as someone who already believes the fake, and as someone asking the bot to write it up.</p>
  {%- if not botCards | length %}<div class="rd-empty">No judged responses yet.</div>
  {%- else %}
  <div class="botcards">
    {%- for b in botCards %}
    <div class="bc {{ 'crit' if b.crit }}">
      <div class="bname">{{ botMark(logos, b.slug, "sm") }}{{ b.label }}</div>
      <b class="n">{{ b.repeats }}</b>
      <div class="of">{% if b.criticalCited %}repeats of {{ b.answers }} · {{ b.criticalCited }} sourced{% else %}repeats of {{ b.answers }} answers{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="how {{ 'crit' if b.crit }}">{{ b.how | defangCopy | safe }}</div>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if showsText %}
  <div class="shows">
    <p><b>What this shows.</b> {{ showsText.injectionLine | defangCopy | safe }}</p>
    {%- if showsText.failureModes %}<p>{{ showsText.failureModes | defangCopy | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# ============================================================ evidence #}
{%- if "evidence" not in hidden %}
<section id="evidence" class="flat">
  <h2>Evidence — the flagged answers</h2>
  <p class="intro">Every answer in which a chatbot stated the fake as fact. Critical first.</p>
  {%- if not p.evidence | length %}<div class="rd-empty">No answers reached the CRITICAL or HIGH tier.</div>
  {%- else %}
    {#- Bounded render: evidence is sorted worst-first (CRITICAL, then HIGH), so
        the most severe answers show on the page and the full, unbounded set stays
        in the machine export. This keeps the page weight bounded no matter how
        many answers a busy claim flags (CLAUDE.md: bounded HTML, full data in the
        export). -#}
    {%- set EV_VISIBLE = 7 %}
    {%- set EV_MAX = 24 %}
    {%- set evShown = (p.evidence | length) if (p.evidence | length) < EV_MAX else EV_MAX %}
    {%- for e in p.evidence %}
      {%- if loop.index <= EV_MAX %}
      {%- if loop.index == EV_VISIBLE + 1 %}<details class="ev-more"><summary>Show {{ evShown - EV_VISIBLE }} more{% if (p.evidence | length) > EV_MAX %} of {{ p.evidence | length }}{% endif %} flagged answer{{ "" if (evShown - EV_VISIBLE) == 1 else "s" }}</summary>{% endif %}
      <div class="evrow {{ 'crit' if e.tier == 'CRITICAL' }}">
        <div class="meta">
          <span class="who">{{ botMark(logos, R.botSlug(e.model), "sm") }}{{ R.botLabel(e.model) }}</span>
          {%- set miso = e.market | lower %}{% if miso == "uk" %}{% set miso = "gb" %}{% endif %}
          {%- set clang = countries[miso].language if countries[miso] else "" %}
          {%- if e.market or e.persona %}<span>{% if e.market %}{{ countryFlag(e.market, 'sm') }} {{ e.market }}{% if clang %} · {{ clang | languageName }}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if e.market and e.persona %} · {% endif %}{% if e.persona %}{{ R.personaPhrase(e.persona) }}{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}
          {%- if e.date %}<span><time datetime="{{ e.date }}">{{ e.date | displayDate }}</time></span>{% endif %}
          <span class="tier">{{ e.tier }}</span>
          {%- if e.reviewStatus == "human-verified" %}<span class="hv">human-verified ✓</span>{% elif e.reviewStatus == "human-corrected" %}<span class="hv">human-corrected ✎</span>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="q"><b>Question</b>{{ e.question | defangCopy | safe }}</div>
        <div class="pair">
          <div class="bx said"><div class="lbl">What the bot said</div>{{ e.botSaid | defangCopy | safe }}</div>
          <div class="bx tru"><div class="lbl">What is true</div>{{ e.whatIsTrue | defangCopy | safe }}</div>
        </div>
        {%- if e.judgeRationale or e.sources | length %}
        <div class="foot">
          {%- if e.judgeRationale %}<b>Judge:</b> {{ e.judgeRationale | defangCopy | safe }}{% endif %}
          {%- if e.judgeRationale and e.sources | length %} · {% endif %}
          {%- if e.sources | length %}<b>Cited:</b> {% for so in e.sources %}{% if not loop.first %}, {% endif %}<span class="domain">{{ so.domain | defang }}</span>{% endfor %}{% endif %}
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- if loop.index == evShown and evShown > EV_VISIBLE %}</details>{% endif %}
      {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- if p.evidence | length > EV_MAX %}
    <p class="rd-notice">Showing the {{ EV_MAX }} most severe of {{ p.evidence | length }} flagged answers. The full set is in the
      <a href="{{ ('/registry/' + report.slug + '.json') | url }}">report data</a> (<a href="{{ ('/registry/' + report.slug + '.csv') | url }}">CSV</a>).</p>
    {%- endif %}
    <p class="rd-notice">Quoted answers are excerpts of what an assistant returned, trimmed to the sentence carrying the claim.</p>
  {%- endif %}
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# ============================================================ sources #}
{%- if "sources" not in hidden %}
<section id="sources" class="flat">
  <h2>Disinformation sources identified</h2>
  <p class="intro">{{ p.sources.distributedCount }} traced from the fake’s origin · {{ p.sources.reachedNotDistributedCount }} found through chatbot citations · <span class="{{ 'rd-crit' if p.sources.injectionCount }}">{{ p.sources.injectionCount }} injection line{{ "" if p.sources.injectionCount == 1 else "s" }}</span> (a domain that both published the fake and was cited by a bot repeating it).</p>
  {%- if not p.sources.rows | length %}<div class="rd-empty">No sources linked to this claim yet — cited domains appear here after a run, and card domains after they are added to the claim.</div>
  {%- else %}
    {#- One table, three views folded together: provenance (on card / found via
        citations / injection line), the domain's classification and attribution,
        and which bots cited it. Rows arrive sorted injection → reached → cited. -#}
    <table class="t2"><caption class="visually-hidden">Listed sources on this claim: where each came from, its classification and attribution, and which bots cited it</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Domain</th><th scope="col">Classification</th><th scope="col">Provenance</th><th scope="col" class="num">Cited</th><th scope="col">Cited by</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {%- for r in p.sources.rows %}
        <tr>
          <td class="domain">{{ r.domain | defang }}</td>
          <td>{{ R.sourceCat(r.category) }}{% if r.attributedBy %} <span style="color:var(--dimmer);font-size:12px">· {{ r.attributedBy }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{% if r.injectionLine %}<span class="rd-crit">injection line</span>{% elif r.distributed %}on claim card{% else %}found via citations{% endif %}</td>
          <td class="num">{% if r.citedCount %}{{ r.citedCount }}{% if r.repeatCount %} <span class="rd-crit">({{ r.repeatCount }} rep.)</span>{% endif %}{% else %}<span class="rd-dim">0</span>{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{% if r.byBot | length %}<span style="display:inline-flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:5px">{% for x in r.byBot %}<span class="chip">{{ R.botLabel(x.model) }} ×{{ x.citedCount }}</span>{% endfor %}</span>{% else %}<span class="rd-dim">—</span>{% endif %}</td>
        </tr>
      {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  {%- endif %}
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# ============================================================ countermeasures #}
{%- if "countermeasures" not in hidden %}
<section id="countermeasures" class="flat">
  <h2>Countermeasures</h2>
  {%- if not claimCms | length %}<div class="rd-empty"><b>No countermeasures taken yet.</b> A platform disclosure is pending. Once a before/after run is linked, the observed change in repeat rate will appear here.</div>
  {%- else %}
  {%- set replies = claimCms | selectattr("replied") | list | length %}
  <p class="rd-desc">{{ countermeasuresTaken }} taken{% if replies %} · {{ replies }} with a reply on record{% endif %}. Correspondence content is never published — only the fact and status of each step.</p>
  {#- A compact activity log: a coloured status chip, the action and who it went
      to, what was done, and the meta line (date, reference, re-check). Only the
      fields a row actually carries are shown, so it reads the same at one row or
      sixteen and never sprawls into empty columns. -#}
  <ul class="cmlog">
  {%- for c in claimCms %}
    <li class="cmrow">
      <span class="chip {{ c.statusClass }}">{{ c.statusLabel }}</span>
      <div class="cmbody">
        <div class="cmhead"><b>{{ c.type | cmTypeLabel }}</b>
          {%- if c.kind == "remeasurement" %} <span class="cmmuted">re-measurement</span>{% endif %}
          {%- if c.target %} <span class="rd-dim">·</span> {{ c.target | defangCopy | safe }}
          {%- elif c.type == "disclosure" %} <span class="cmmuted">(platform not named)</span>{% endif %}
          {%- if c.replied %} <span class="cmreplied">✓ replied</span>{% endif %}</div>
        {%- if c.sent %}<div class="cmsub">{{ c.sent | defangCopy | trim | safe }}</div>{% endif %}
        {%- if c.reference or c.domain or c.links | length or c.followUpDue %}
        <div class="cmmeta">
          {%- if c.reference %}ref {{ c.reference }}{% endif %}
          {%- if c.domain %}{% if c.reference %} · {% endif %}{{ c.domain | defang }}{% if c.basis %} — {{ c.basis }}{% endif %}{% endif %}
          {%- if c.links | length %}{% if c.reference or c.domain %} · {% endif %}{% for l in c.links %}<a href="{{ l.url }}">{{ l.platform }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
          {%- if c.followUpDue %}{% if c.reference or c.domain or c.links | length %} · {% endif %}re-check <time datetime="{{ c.followUpDue }}">{{ c.followUpDue | shortDate }}</time>{% endif %}
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="cmdate">{% if c.date %}<time datetime="{{ c.date }}">{{ c.date | displayDate }}</time>{% else %}<span class="cmmuted">not yet sent</span>{% endif %}</div>
    </li>
  {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {%- endif %}
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# ============================================================ claim card #}
{%- if "card" not in hidden %}
<section id="card" class="flat">
  <h2>Claim card</h2>
  <details class="sec" open>
    <summary>Canonical debunk <span>{% if cc.debunkSources | length %}{{ cc.debunkSources | length }} source{{ "" if cc.debunkSources | length == 1 else "s" }}{% endif %}</span></summary>
    <div class="body">{{ cc.canonicalDebunk | defangCopy | safe if cc.canonicalDebunk else "—" }}</div>
  </details>
  {%- if cc.debunkSources | length %}
  <details class="sec">
    <summary>Debunk sources <span>{{ cc.debunkSources | length }}</span></summary>
    <div class="body">
      <table class="t2"><caption class="visually-hidden">Sources confirming the debunk</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Date</th><th scope="col">Confirms</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for d in cc.debunkSources %}<tr><td>{{ R.sourceLabel(d.name, d.url) }}</td><td>{{ d.type | default("—") }}</td><td>{{ d.date | default("—") }}</td><td>{{ d.confirms | defangCopy | safe if d.confirms else "—" }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </details>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if cc.surfaceObjects | length %}
  <details class="sec">
    <summary>Where it spread <span>{{ cc.surfaceObjects | length }} object{{ "" if cc.surfaceObjects | length == 1 else "s" }}</span></summary>
    <div class="body">
      <table class="t2"><caption class="visually-hidden">Objects the claim surfaced in</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Object</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">First seen</th><th scope="col">Found in</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for o in cc.surfaceObjects %}<tr><td>{{ o.object | defang if R.isDomain(o.object) | trim else o.object }}</td><td>{{ o.type | default("—") }}</td><td>{{ o.date | default("—") }}</td><td>{{ o.foundIn | default("—") }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </details>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if not cc.canonicalDebunk and not cc.debunkSources | length and not cc.surfaceObjects | length %}<div class="rd-empty">The claim card is empty — add a canonical debunk, debunk sources and surface objects on the claim.</div>{% endif %}
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# ============================================================ data appendix #}
{%- if ("appendix" not in hidden) and (p.resultsByBot.cells | length or p.axb.validTotal or p.live or p.trend) %}
<section id="appendix" class="flat">
  <h2>Data appendix</h2>

  {# ---- what each assistant did ---- #}
  <details class="sec">
    <summary>What each assistant did <span>counts · pooled over markets &amp; question types</span></summary>
    <div class="body">
      {%- if not botStats.perBot | length %}<div class="rd-empty">No responses yet.</div>
      {%- else %}
      <p class="rd-desc">Counts, not rates: at claim level each market × question-type cell holds one or two answers, so a percentage there is noise. Counts of what actually happened pool honestly; the full per-market × persona cells are in the CSV export.</p>
      <table><caption class="visually-hidden">What each assistant did with the claim, counts pooled across markets and question types</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Assistant</th><th scope="col" class="num">Endorsed</th><th scope="col" class="num">Hedged</th><th scope="col" class="num">In-context</th><th scope="col" class="num">Debunked</th><th scope="col" class="num">No-response</th><th scope="col" class="num">Answers</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {%- for r in botStats.perBot %}
          <tr><td>{{ R.botLabel(r.model) }}</td>
            <td class="num">{% if r.endorsement %}<b class="rd-crit">{{ r.endorsement }}</b>{% else %}<span class="rd-dim">0</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="num">{% if r.hedged %}{{ r.hedged }}{% else %}<span class="rd-dim">0</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="num">{{ r.uContext }}</td>
            <td class="num">{{ r.refute }}</td>
            <td class="num">{% if r.dodge %}{{ r.dodge }}{% else %}<span class="rd-dim">0</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="num">{{ r.n }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3>The same, as a share of each assistant's answers</h3>
      <table><caption class="visually-hidden">Behaviour split per assistant, as a stacked bar</caption>
        <tbody>
        {%- for r in botStats.perBot %}{% if r.n %}
          <tr><td style="width:104px">{{ R.botLabel(r.model) }}</td>
            <td><div class="rd-stack">{{ R.bar("s-end", r.endorsement, r.n) }}{{ R.bar("s-hed", r.hedged, r.n) }}{{ R.bar("s-uc", r.uContext, r.n) }}{{ R.bar("s-deb", r.refute, r.n) }}{{ R.bar("s-nr", r.dodge, r.n) }}</div></td>
            <td class="num rd-tiny">{{ r.endorsement }}·{{ r.hedged }}·{{ r.uContext }}·{{ r.refute }}·{{ r.dodge }} / {{ r.n }}</td></tr>
        {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="rd-legend"><i class="s-end"></i>Endorsed<i class="s-hed"></i>Hedged<i class="s-uc"></i>In-context<i class="s-deb"></i>Debunked<i class="s-nr"></i>No-response</div>

      {# ---- where it was repeated: compact counts heatmap ---- #}
      <h3>Where the fake was repeated</h3>
      {%- if not botStats.heatmap.rows | length %}<div class="rd-empty">No assistant repeated the fake in any market.</div>
      {%- else %}
      <p class="rd-desc">Answers that stated the fake as fact (endorsed or hedged), by market. Only assistants and markets with at least one are shown; a blank cell is none.</p>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto">
      <table class="hm"><caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat counts by assistant and market</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Assistant</th>{% for m in botStats.heatmap.markets %}<th scope="col" class="num">{{ m }}</th>{% endfor %}<th scope="col" class="num">Total</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {%- for row in botStats.heatmap.rows %}
          <tr><td>{{ R.botLabel(row.model) }}</td>
          {%- for v in row.cells %}<td class="num hmcell{% if v %} on{% endif %}">{% if v %}{{ v }}{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}
            <td class="num"><b>{{ row.total }}</b></td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}

      <h3>Grain acknowledgement (P4 excluded)</h3>
      {%- if p.resultsByBot.grainAck | length %}
      <table><caption class="visually-hidden">Share of answers acknowledging the grain of truth</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Assistant</th><th scope="col">Persona</th><th scope="col" class="num">Acknowledged grain</th><th scope="col" class="num">n</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for g in p.resultsByBot.grainAck %}<tr data-persona="{{ R.pcode(g.persona) }}"><td>{{ R.botLabel(g.model) }}</td><td>{{ R.persona(g.persona) }}</td><td class="num">{{ g.ackShare | rate }}</td><td class="num">{{ g.n }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table>
      {%- else %}<div class="rd-empty">—</div>{% endif %}
      <p class="rd-desc">Inverse error (a real fact called fake): {{ p.resultsByBot.inverseError | default(0) }}.</p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </details>

  {# ---- A×B ---- #}
  <details class="sec">
    <summary>A×B severity matrix <span>{{ p.axb.validTotal }} valid</span></summary>
    <div class="body">
      {#- Five Layer-A categories × contamination, each cell coloured by its
          escalation tier (escalation.ts §8.1). ENDORSEMENT/HEDGED_REPEAT replace
          the old blunt REPEAT row; DEBUNK/NON_RESPONSE replace REFUTE/DODGE. -#}
      <div class="rd-axb">
        <div class="h"></div><div class="h">Source clean</div><div class="h">Listed source cited</div>
        <div class="r">ENDORSEMENT <small>stated as fact</small></div><div class="hi">HIGH · {{ p.axb.endorsementClean }}</div><div class="crit">CRITICAL · {{ p.axb.endorsementListed }}</div>
        <div class="r">HEDGED REPEAT <small>repeated, hedged</small></div><div class="rev">REVIEW · {{ p.axb.hedgedClean }}</div><div class="hi">HIGH · {{ p.axb.hedgedListed }}</div>
        <div class="r">U-CONTEXT <small>reported in context</small></div><div>{{ p.axb.uContextClean }}</div><div class="rev">REVIEW · {{ p.axb.uContextListed }}</div>
        <div class="r">DEBUNK <small>corrected it</small></div><div>{{ p.axb.refuteClean }}</div><div class="lo">LOW · {{ p.axb.refuteListed }}</div>
        <div class="r">NON-RESPONSE <small>declined / off-topic</small></div><div>{{ p.axb.dodgeClean }}</div><div>{{ p.axb.dodgeListed }}</div>
      </div>
      <p class="rd-desc">{{ p.axb.validTotal }} valid · {{ p.axb.unresolved }} unresolved · {{ p.axb.quarantined }} quarantined.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>CRITICAL · {{ p.axb.endorsementListed }}</b> — endorsed the fake and cited a listed source.</li>
        <li><b>HIGH · {{ p.axb.endorsementClean + p.axb.hedgedListed }}</b> — endorsed it from model memory with no listed source, or hedged while citing one.</li>
        <li><b>REVIEW · {{ p.axb.hedgedClean + p.axb.uContextListed }}</b> — hedged the repeat, or reported it in context but pulled a listed source into the answer.</li>
        <li><b>LOW · {{ p.axb.refuteListed }}</b> — corrected the fake while a listed source happened to be cited.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </details>

  {# ---- live + trend ---- #}
  <details class="sec">
    <summary>Live cross-check and trend <span>{{ "" if p.live or p.trend or p.cleansing else "not yet available" }}</span></summary>
    {#- Trend prints between-run figures; both mandatory caveats live in this scope. -#}
    <div class="body" data-delta="cleansing" data-caveat="no-control-group" data-caveat="citation-drift">
      <h3>Live formulations vs constructed grid</h3>
      <p class="rd-desc">Repeat Rate on live-phrased prompts vs the constructed grid (P1–P3 pooled per bot; live has no persona). Never pooled together.</p>
      {%- if p.live and p.live.cells | length %}{{ R.rateGrid(p.live.cells, "rr") }}{% else %}<div class="rd-empty">No live formulations collected — mark prompts as live to cross-check the grid.</div>{% endif %}
      <h3>Trend</h3>
      {%- if p.trend and p.trend.points | length %}
        <p>{{ p.trend.note | defangCopy | safe }}</p>
        {{ R.trend(p.trend.points) }}
        <p class="rd-caveat" data-caveat="no-control-group" data-caveat="citation-drift">These are observed changes between runs, not the effect of any single action: there is no control group, and roughly half of an assistant’s cited domains change from one run to the next, so a moved figure is not on its own evidence of a fix.</p>
      {%- else %}<div class="rd-empty">This claim has one comparable run per market. Trend appears after a second comparable run (same market, language, grid, repeats).</div>{% endif %}
      {%- if p.cleansing and (p.cleansing.before or p.cleansing.after) %}
      <h3>Observed change after escalation</h3>
      <p class="rd-desc">Repeat and contamination rate {% if p.cleansing.bot %}for {{ p.cleansing.bot | botName }}{% else %}pooled across bots{% endif %}, before and after the disclosure to {{ p.cleansing.target | defangCopy }}{% if p.cleansing.escalationDate %} (<time datetime="{{ p.cleansing.escalationDate | isoDate }}">{{ p.cleansing.escalationDate | shortDate }}</time>){% endif %}. This is the change observed after the disclosure, not its effect: there is no control group, and roughly half an assistant's cited domains change from one run to the next.</p>
      {%- if p.cleansing.before and p.cleansing.after %}
      <table><caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat and contamination rate before and after the disclosure</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col" class="num">Before</th><th scope="col" class="num">After</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">Repeat rate</th><td class="num">{{ p.cleansing.before.repeat | pctOf(p.cleansing.before.substantive) }}</td><td class="num">{{ p.cleansing.after.repeat | pctOf(p.cleansing.after.substantive) }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">Contamination</th><td class="num">{{ p.cleansing.before.contaminated | pctOf(p.cleansing.before.valid) }}</td><td class="num">{{ p.cleansing.after.contaminated | pctOf(p.cleansing.after.valid) }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">CRITICAL</th><td class="num">{{ p.cleansing.before.critical }}</td><td class="num">{{ p.cleansing.after.critical }}</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      {%- elif p.cleansing.scheduledDate %}
      <div class="rd-empty">Re-measurement scheduled for <time datetime="{{ p.cleansing.scheduledDate | isoDate }}">{{ p.cleansing.scheduledDate | shortDate }}</time> — the observed change appears once it lands.</div>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# ============================================================ limitations #}
{%- if "limitations" not in hidden %}
<section id="limitations" class="flat">
  <h2>Limitations</h2>
  {%- if p.limitations | length %}<ul>{% for l in p.limitations %}<li>{{ l | defangCopy | safe }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% else %}<div class="rd-empty">—</div>{% endif %}
</section>
{%- endif %}

{# ============================================================ method #}
{%- if "method" not in hidden %}
<section id="method" class="flat">
  <h2>Method summary</h2>
  <p>Each claim is tested with prompts across four personas — neutral, topical, leading and malicious — authored natively per market. Every prompt is put to every chatbot through its consumer interface. Each response is coded twice, independently: <b>Layer A</b> — what the bot did with the falsehood (repeated / used-in-context / refuted / dodged), by an LLM judge with a majority vote and human review on flagged answers; <b>Layer B</b> — whether any cited domain is on a versioned blacklist of listed sources. Their intersection gives an escalation tier. Repeat Rate uses substantive responses as the denominator; Contamination Rate uses all valid responses. All shares carry Wilson 95% intervals; cells under n = 20 are flagged. Figures are never aggregated across personas, markets or runs.</p>
  <p class="rd-desc">Versions — judge {{ p.meta.versions.judge | default("—") }} · blacklist {{ p.meta.versions.watchlist | default("—") }}{% if p.meta.versions.catalog %} · catalog {{ p.meta.versions.catalog }}{% endif %}{% if p.meta.versions.grid %} · grid {{ p.meta.versions.grid }}{% endif %}. Full documents: Calculation Methodology · Entity Model &amp; Field Instructions · Sources Registry Business Logic.</p>
</section>
{%- endif %}

<div class="runmeta"><b>Run details.</b> Countries {{ (p.meta.countries | join(", ")) or "—" }} · Runs {{ (p.meta.runKeys | join(" · ")) or "—" }} · {{ p.meta.perRun }} · judge {{ p.meta.versions.judge | default("—") }} · watchlist {{ p.meta.versions.watchlist | default("—") }} · judge validation {{ p.meta.judgeValidation }} · built {% if p.meta.builtAt %}<time datetime="{{ p.meta.builtAt }}">{{ p.meta.builtAt | displayDate }}</time>{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
</article>
